# TERMINAL STATE — levels/L3-full-spectrum.lvl
#
# L3 · "Full Spectrum" — the story-true successor to levels/03.lvl (which stays in
# the ARCHIVE folder, golden and untouched).
#
# SPATIAL + GRAPH REBUILD 2026-09-23 (real-world) (the spatial redesign §3 L3,
# the puzzle-graph redesign §L3). Identity: a cold spectrometry room
# with an iron mezzanine: three coloured lamps mix on the floor, snow falls
# through the double height, and your own handwriting waits at the foot of the
# stair.
#
# SPACE: resized 18x16x5 -> 18x16x9 (LOCKED node/pipe/switch/door coordinates are
# unchanged — they all still fit the original x,y footprint). A north-wall
# MEZZANINE (slab z=5, walk z=6..7, over y=1..2, x=9..16) is reached by a new
# straight 5-tread stair on y=1 from x=4 (`storey_height = 5`), landing (9,1,5).
# The mezzanine footprint is clear of every pipe cell (the lowest service run is
# y=3), so this is a pure ADD, not a reroute. `[cells]` is therefore authored for
# the first time on this level: every one of the seven pipes' `render_pipes`
# traces is repainted cell-for-cell as WallTrace so the network stays exactly as
# visible as it was as a flat auto-boxed room (see L1's own header for why an
# authored `[cells]` grid must repaint a path or it silently goes invisible).
# Spawn moves upstairs to (9,1,6) facing +y — right at the stair landing, so
# frame 1 looks down over the whole room before the player takes the stair down
# to wire the floor. (Round-2 dressing moved it to the walkway's east end, (16,2,6)
# yaw 390 — see [player].)
#
# FIX (real-world) (2026-09-23, found by `cold_levels_render_visible_snow_in_a_
# dump_frame`): the brief's own (14,2,6) put the mezzanine camera near the EAST
# edge of the walkway, most of the room's synthesized snow lattice (`re_level::
# snow_emitters`, a fixed 3x4x4 grid over the whole room interior) fell outside
# its forward view, and only 14 flake cells read in the dump frame against the
# CANON `snow = 0.4` (LOCKED, do not raise it — the spatial redesign §3 L3 "Keep").
# The landing (9,1,6) is the same upstairs vantage, same facing, same "look down
# before you descend" beat — just centred over the room's x-span instead of
# offset toward one wall — and clears the threshold (21-24 flake cells measured).
#
# GRAPH (the puzzle-graph redesign §L3 — overrides the shipped defect where they
# conflict): the shipped graph let the WRONG hidden node (h2, "the second hidden
# node... it remembers the wrong room") also open the door in 3 toggles, so the
# note's "make magenta" was advice, not a rule. Fix: `h2` threshold 2 -> 1 (so the
# glazed-over false memory is just as easy to reach, and just as clearly wrong),
# and `[door] target_parts = output h1` (the door now also requires the TRUE
# memory h1, not just the base `output`). The emit is split so the player SEES
# which memory they built: `output=1` lights the base for any colour, `h1=1`
# lights the magenta X (the true memory), `h2=1` lights a new teal diamond (the
# false one). Node positions, all seven pipe paths/switches, `power_budget = 3`,
# and every note text are UNCHANGED — LOCKED.
#
# Fix D1 (the spatial redesign §1): `ambient` trace-pattern -> solid, so the room's
# `wall_solid`/`floor` materials actually paint instead of the inert
# `live_trace` binding. The wall material moves off `preset = ice` (reflective —
# would turn this into an unintended mirror, invariant 7) onto an explicit
# `recipe = circuit` with the same ice-blue colours; the floor moves off the
# self-lit `metal` preset onto a LIT `grain` recipe so the three lamp-pools
# actually show on it.
#
# CAMPAIGN SLOT: manifest #3 · movement P1 "First Sight" · load ▃
#   **TWIST 1 lands here** — and PROGRESSION §1 puts it in a deliberately LOW
#   cognitive valley so the player has spare attention to feel the dread. Every
#   individual solve is easy; the level's demand is BREADTH, not depth.
#
# NEW IDEA (exactly one): **truth-table breadth** — three input bits, eight worlds.
#   "3 bits = 8 worlds. I contain more than I was shown."
#
# ── MECHANIC (pure data — two hidden detectors over three inputs) ─────────────
#   R (IN=1) ─┬──────────────►  h1 MAGENTA (T=2)  ─┐
#             └──(long arc)──►  h2 TEAL    (T=1)  ─┤
#   G (IN=1) ────────────────►  h2 TEAL    (T=1)  ─┼─►  output (T=1) ─► door (needs output AND h1)
#   B (IN=1) ─┬──────────────►  h1 MAGENTA (T=2)  ─┘
#             └──────────────►  h2 TEAL    (T=1)
#
# Eight reachable input worlds; the door wants MAGENTA. h1 fires on R+B (the full
# spectrum closing); h2 (threshold 1, the puzzle-graph redesign §L3) fires on any ONE of
# R/G/B and is the SECOND HIDDEN NODE the unsigned note warns about — "don't trust
# the second hidden node when B is high. it remembers the wrong room." h2 can
# still light `output`, but the door ALSO requires h1 (`target_parts = output h1`),
# so h2's route lights the base and the wrong teal diamond and the door stays
# shut: a *legal*-looking but losing solve that gives you the wrong colour and the
# wrong memory: TEAL, MIST, GLAZE — the glazed-over look of a false recollection.
#
# SOLUTION (3 toggles): R->h1 ON, B->h1 ON, h1->output ON. Minimum 3, unique.
#   (h2 also reaches `output` in as little as 1-2 toggles, but never the door —
#    the discipline the level teaches is choosing the RIGHT hidden node, and the
#    note is how you know which. The colour of the emitted block is the verdict.)
#
# READOUT (WORD_STORY §RESULT, canon): FIRE + SEA -> MAGENTA -> MODEL   — A.
# NAME SHARD 3: the initial `A` — from an unsigned note in your own hand.
#
# ── TOKEN DISCIPLINE (W1 allowlist) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The duplicate-handle log uses `{time}` — an ALLOWLISTED Tier-1 alias of
# `{local_time}` — on its own line, so it resolves in both opt states and never
# drops. `tail.log modified 2026-06-18 03:14` is a LITERAL future mtime
# (STORY_BIBLE §7 "Future mtime"); the real `{last_file}` read is A-7-permitted
# only at L12, so nothing is interpolated for it here. FORM 12 and FORM 03 carry
# no tokens at all.
#
# Verify:
#   cargo run -q -p re_game -- --dump levels/L3-full-spectrum.lvl --ansi
#   cargo run -q -p re_lvlcheck --bin lvlcheck -- levels/L3-full-spectrum.lvl

[meta]
name        = level-L3-full-spectrum
title       = Full Spectrum
version     = 1
spec_rev    = 2026-09-23
prop_style  = lab

[room]
size        = 18 16 9
floor       = grid
ceiling     = dim
ambient     = solid
storey_height = 5
# POWER BUDGET (v0.2 re-scope, user-approved 2026-08-05). At most N pipes may be
# ON at the same time; switching one ON at the cap is REFUSED (the pipe stays off
# and nothing else changes), switching one OFF always frees a unit. Absent or 0 =
# unlimited, which is what every non-campaign level still carries.
# WHY: the forward pass has no inhibition, so activation is MONOTONE in the ON-set
# — without a cap, all-switches-ON wins whenever anything wins, and every decoy in
# the campaign is decorative. This is the number that makes wrong wiring cost.
# THIS LEVEL: 3 of 7 pipes. One hidden node has to reach threshold 2 and then reach the
# output: e.g. R->h2 + G->h2 + h2->output. Four of the seven wires are slack the
# player does not have. Lighting the whole spectrum is now exactly the wrong move.
power_budget = 3
# Draw the puzzle NETWORK. Without this the pipes the player actually manipulates
# are invisible wiring: no flow scroll, no powered-hue lift, no streaming node
# word-pool, and no switch-toggle / cycle-reject event pulse has a surface to
# appear on. Traces stamp into EMPTY air only, so no geometry is clobbered.
render_pipes = true

# ── ESCALATION (manifest fog_far = 17.0) ──────────────────────────────────────
# **The cold begins here.** `snow = 0.4` and `fog_color = #101826` are the CANON
# L3 values (STORY_BIBLE §5 L3: "холодный туман + снег — комната, которую заметка
# помнит неправильно"): degradation becomes visible for the first time. fog_far
# steps down from L2's 19.0 — the world starts closing in. Still no matrix bleed:
# the corruption ramp starts at L4, so the cold arrives BEFORE the rot.
[effects]
snow        = 0.4

[palette]
fog_color   = #101826
fog_near    = 2.5
fog_far     = 17.0

# ── LIGHTING (the spatial redesign) ───────────────────────────────────
# Lamp count = the count of what you are learning: L3 has 3 (RGB, "three bits").
# z raised 3.6 -> 4.6 vs the brief's number: the brief's z=3.6 was calibrated for
# the OLD 5-tall room (ceiling at z=4); this room is now double-height and the
# x=5 column at z=3 is where the puzzle-graph redesign's `R->h2`/`B->h1` pipes climb to
# the elevated service layer (LOCKED path), so a lamp at the brief's exact
# position sits buried inside that WallTrace geometry (lvlcheck `lighting` WARN).
# z=4.6 clears it — still low, still reads as "over the switch/input row".
[light]
pos         = 5.0, 3.0, 4.6
color       = #FF4040
radius      = 4.5
intensity   = 1.0

[light]
pos         = 5.0, 8.0, 4.6
color       = #40FF40
radius      = 4.5
intensity   = 0.8

[light]
pos         = 5.0, 13.0, 4.6
color       = #4080FF
radius      = 4.5
intensity   = 1.0

[atmosphere]
ambient     = 0.10
key_color   = #405070
postfx      = clean

# ── COLOR-FORWARD palette ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A neon chamber going cold: ice-blue masonry (the room the note remembers wrong),
# a steel deck, and near-black overhead. The live wire is violet — the spectrum
# closing on the colour of the bruise. Fix D1: `ambient = solid` means these
# perimeter walls actually paint now; the wall moves OFF `preset = ice` (which is
# reflective — invariant 7, would turn this into an unintended mirror) onto an
# explicit `recipe = circuit` with the same colours, and the floor moves off the
# self-lit `metal` preset onto a LIT `grain` recipe so the three lamp-pools show.
[material spectrum_wall]
fg          = #6EA0D8
bg          = #070C16
recipe      = circuit scale=1.6
surface     = wall_solid

[material spectrum_floor]
fg          = #5F6C82
bg          = #080C14
recipe      = grain scale=3.0 speck=0.15
surface     = floor

[material spectrum_ceiling]
preset      = metal
fg          = #2A3040
bg          = #04050A
surface     = ceiling

[material live_trace]
preset      = neon
fg          = #E070E0
bg          = #140818
surface     = wall_trace

# ── DENSE [cells] GRID (the spatial redesign) ─────────────────────────
# 18 cols (x=0..17) x 16 rows (y=0..15) x 9 z-layers. z=0 floor slab, z=1..4 the
# lower hall (double height), z=5 the mezzanine slab (+ the 5 stair treads and
# landing), z=6..7 the mezzanine walk, z=8 ceiling. `render_pipes` tags every
# path cell's side_data BEFORE this grid stamps (order: stamp_pipes -> [cells]),
# and `[cells]` PRESERVES side_data while it is authoritative for KIND — so every
# `/` painted below is one of the seven pipes' own expanded path cells (switch
# cells included), reproducing exactly what the flat auto-boxed room used to show
# implicitly. The six node cells (R,G,B,h1,h2,output) and the door are
# deliberately left as air here; nodes auto-restore to Object (they are Empty in
# this grid), matching L1's own convention.
[cells]
size        = 18 16 9

